+# F-29: Tend UI View Switcher
+
+## Result
+
+Status: `[x] complete`
+
+The card/table mode control now renders through Tend UI `Segmented` with packaged `CardView` and `TableView` icons.
+
+## Ownership Contract
+
+React owns only the visual segmented control and its selected indicator.
+
+`src/ui/basic-controls.js` remains the application-state owner:
+
+1. React emits `s-tracker:view-request` with `cards` or `table`.
+2. Vanilla code validates the requested value.
+3. Vanilla code switches `#view-mode-cards` and `#view-mode-table`.
+4. Vanilla code updates column/download action visibility.
+5. Vanilla code records `data-current-view` and emits `s-tracker:view-changed`.
+6. React synchronizes the selected segment from that confirmed event.
+
+The adapter contains no task rendering, column state, download behavior or navigation logic.
+
+## Public Package Export
+
+F-29 exposed an existing component through a missing narrow package export:
+
+```text
+@10d/tend-ui/primitives/Segmented
+```
+
+The export provides ESM, CJS and type entrypoints. The main package was rebuilt, public metadata was checked, the local tarball was refreshed and S-Tracker's lockfile now records the new tarball integrity.
+
+This avoids the aggregate `@10d/tend-ui/primitives` import, which would have increased the S-Tracker JavaScript bundle from approximately `747 KB` to `1.61 MB`.
+
